 and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** The first rollback to v2.3.0 stopped partway because of an orchestrator error. Only us-east had changed, so regions were running different versions. I retried once and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks are passing and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) covers the failing release, both rollback attempts and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find what broke in v2.3.1, and find out why the orchestrator stopped the first rollback. The request to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had already been created, so I didn't send it again, and on-call was paged only once.", "type": "text"}]}]}